WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.894
Chapter 17. Automated checks, browser acceptance, and criteria. Acceptance covers file presence, structure, hashes, media streams, caption timelines, document containers, language switching, playback, and downloads. An automated pass is not a human accessibility, mobile, or production pass.

2
00:00:27.214 --> 00:00:53.989
verify.py checks 18 chapters, 36 chapter audio files, 72 SRT/VTT files, 36 transcripts, figure and download paths, manifest hashes, codecs and durations, monotonic caption timing, PDF/DOCX/EPUB/ZIP containers, JavaScript syntax, and browser self-tests.

3
00:00:54.309 --> 00:01:16.279
Browser self-tests run in headless Chrome/Edge and switch languages while checking body text, navigation, captions, download labels, audio source, track language, speed, progress, current subtitle, chapter changes, and external network requests.

4
00:01:16.599 --> 00:01:41.933
Human acceptance still covers keyboard order, visible focus, screen readers, mobile width, print output, Windows high contrast, narration quality, publication rights, and production endpoints. Unperformed items remain pending in verification.json; external release results are recorded in deployment and online acceptance reports.

5
00:01:42.253 --> 00:01:53.720
Automated: structure, media, hashes, captions, containers, syntax.

6
00:01:54.040 --> 00:02:05.783
Browser: switching, playback, progress, subtitles, chapters, offline.

7
00:02:06.103 --> 00:02:15.675
Human: accessibility, mobile, content, rights.

8
00:02:15.995 --> 00:02:29.017
External production: URLs, authentication, rate limits, and deployed resources, as evidenced by the online acceptance report.

9
00:02:29.337 --> 00:02:45.019
Try one step: Run python verify.py --browser and inspect every detail in verification.json. Do not treat summary.ok alone as complete acceptance.
